✅ Step-by-Step: Enable GStreamer in OpenCV on macOS



brew install cmake pkg-config
brew install gstreamer gst-plugins-base gst-plugins-good gst-plugins-bad gst-plugins-ugly
brew install ffmpeg



📥 Step 1: Download OpenCV

cd ~
git clone https://github.com/opencv/opencv.git
git clone https://github.com/opencv/opencv_contrib.git

You can checkout a specific stable version (e.g., 4.8.0) if you prefer:

=
cd opencv && git checkout 4.8.0 && cd ..
cd opencv_contrib && git checkout 4.8.0 && cd ..

🏗️ Step 2: Build OpenCV with GStreamer
	`

mkdir -p ~/opencv/build && cd ~/opencv/build



Run CMake with GStreamer support:

b
cmake \
  -D CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=RELEASE \
  -D CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/usr/local \
  -D OPENCV_EXTRA_MODULES_PATH=~/opencv_contrib/modules \
  -D WITH_GSTREAMER=ON \
  -D WITH_FFMPEG=ON \
  -D BUILD_opencv_python3=ON \
  -D BUILD_EXAMPLES=OFF \
  ..
✅ Look for the line: -- GStreamer: YES

⚙️ Step 3: Build and Install

make -j$(sysctl -n hw.ncpu)
sudo make install



🐍 Step 4: Link Python to the New OpenCV

cd ~/opencv/build/lib/python3*/site-packages/
cp cv2*.so <your_virtualenv>/lib/python3*/site-packages/
Or install with pip using wheel:


cd ~/opencv/build
make install
cd python_loader
python3 setup.py bdist_wheel
pip install dist/*.whl

✅ Final Check

python3 -c "import cv2; print(cv2.getBuildInformation())" | grep -i gstreamer
You should now see:

yaml

GStreamer: YES
